{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.SWJacksonMomentFactorization","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SWJacksonMomentFactorization","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.NatPowAssoc","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.GeomSum","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Ring.GeomSum","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Regular","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Abel","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SWJacksonMomentFactorization.balancedNormalizer_eq_gauss_mul_jackson","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SWJacksonMomentFactorization.balancedNormalizer_eq_gauss_mul_jackson","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SWJacksonMomentFactorization.lean#L129-L138","doc":"Division form of the factorization: `m_k = G_k · J_k` literally,\nunder the nondegeneracy `1 − p ≠ 0` (i.e. `q ≠ 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SWJacksonMomentFactorization.balancedNormalizer_mul_one_sub_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SWJacksonMomentFactorization.balancedNormalizer_mul_one_sub_pow","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SWJacksonMomentFactorization.lean#L105-L127","doc":"**The SW ⊛ Jackson factorization at moment level** (division-free):\n`N^bal(k+1) · (1−p)^k = v^{C(k,2)} · (p;p)_k` with `p = (v²)⁻¹`. The\nfactor `v^{C(k,2)} = q̃^{k(k−1)/2}` is the moment sequence `G_k` of the\nlog-normal `LN(−L/2, L)` — Stieltjes' 1894 indeterminate example at\nbase `q̃ = √q`, the KSel-3 \"one Gaussian\" — and `(p;p)_k/(1−p)^k` is\nthe Jackson moment sequence `J_k`. So `m_k = G_k · J_k` exactly:\nthe balanced family's indeterminacy core IS the classical SW\nlog-normal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SWJacksonMomentFactorization.qfact_mul_one_sub_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SWJacksonMomentFactorization.qfact_mul_one_sub_pow","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SWJacksonMomentFactorization.lean#L81-L103","doc":"**The q-Laguerre rewrite of the one-sided q-factorial**\n(division-free): `[k]_q! · (1−p)^k = q^{C(k,2)} · (p;p)_k` at `p = q⁻¹`.\nEquivalently `[k]_q! = p^{−C(k,2)}(p;p)_k/(1−p)^k` — the α = 0\nq-Laguerre (generalized Stieltjes–Wigert) moment family under the pure\nscaling `s ↦ (p/(1−p))·s` (`moak1981`; audit §1, EXACT verdict). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SWJacksonMomentFactorization.qint_mul_one_sub_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SWJacksonMomentFactorization.qint_mul_one_sub_inv","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SWJacksonMomentFactorization.lean#L74-L79","doc":"Base-`p` rewrite of one quantum integer: `[k+1]_q · (1−q⁻¹) =\nq^k · (1 − q^{−(k+1)})` — the single-index step behind Moak's\nq-Laguerre scaling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SWJacksonMomentFactorization.qint_mul_one_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SWJacksonMomentFactorization.qint_mul_one_sub","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SWJacksonMomentFactorization.lean#L68-L72","doc":"Telescoped geometric sum: `[n]_p · (1−p) = 1 − p^n` (any `p`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SWJacksonMomentFactorization.pPoch_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SWJacksonMomentFactorization.pPoch_succ","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SWJacksonMomentFactorization.lean#L65-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SWJacksonMomentFactorization.pPoch_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SWJacksonMomentFactorization.pPoch_zero","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SWJacksonMomentFactorization.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SWJacksonMomentFactorization.pPoch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SWJacksonMomentFactorization.pPoch","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SWJacksonMomentFactorization.lean#L57-L61","doc":"The q-Pochhammer `(p;p)_k = ∏_{j=1}^k (1 − p^j)` — the numerator of\nthe Jackson moment sequence. ","signatureChunk":0}]}